<newsitem itemid="65591" id="root" date="1996-09-19" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Wm. Morrison Supermarkets H1 pretax up 8 pct.</title>
<headline>Wm. Morrison Supermarkets H1 pretax up 8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twenty-six weeks to Aug 4</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		4.34		   vs 4.09</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 0.325		  vs 0.275</p>
<p> Pretax		     55.2		   vs 51.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   1.09 billion	 vs 999.7</p>
<p>NOTE - UK food retailer William Morrison Supermarkets Plc said that supermarket takings, including value added tax, had increased in the 26 weeks by 10.5 percent -- or 1.9 percent excluding stores opened since January 1995.</p>
<p> Operating profit	 54.8		   vs 49.7</p>
<p> Loss on disposals	nil		    vs 0.1</p>
<p> Interest receivable    0.4		    vs 1.5</p>
<p> Tax			  21.0		   vs 19.0</p>
<p> Net taxed		  34.2		   vs 32.1</p>
<p> Attributable	     33.4		   vs 31.3</p>
<p> Pay date		   Nov 4</p>
<p> Div registration date  Oct 8</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Sept 30</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that takings in the six weeks since the end of the period, including VAT, had risen 5.6 percent -- or 0.7 percent excluding stores opened since January 1995.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7987</p>
</text>
